<?xpacket begin="Ôªø" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/" x:xmptk="Adobe XMP Core 10.0-c000 1.000000, 0000/00/00-00:00:00        ">
   <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
      <rdf:Description rdf:about=""
            xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
            xmlns:xmp="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/"
            xmlns:xmpMM="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/mm/"
            xmlns:stRef="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/sType/ResourceRef#"
            xmlns:stEvt="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/sType/ResourceEvent#"
            xmlns:pdf="http://ns.adobe.com/pdf/1.3/"
            xmlns:pdfxid="http://www.npes.org/pdfx/ns/id/"
            xmlns:pdfx="http://ns.adobe.com/pdfx/1.3/">
         <dc:format>application/pdf</dc:format>
         <dc:title>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">GSA Field Guide 78 Promotion</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:title>
         <dc:description>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Field Excursions in the Southern Rocky Mountains: From Bedrock to Riverbeds&#xD;Edited by Alexie Millikin and Benjamin J. Laabs&#xD;Five chapters guide you to a variety of geologically interesting routes along the Front Range. First, visit the Laramie anorthosite complex and Sherman batholith to learn about magmatism and mineralization during the assembly of the North American craton. Next, travel to three iconic sites‚ÄîGarden of the Gods, Manitou Springs, and the Cripple Creek District‚Äîto examine the unique geology of the Pikes Peak region. With the third chapter, explore the interplay between uplift and Quaternary glaciation along the boundary of the Front Range and the Great Plains. Next, take a trip to learn how changing alpine environments and water management practices affect streamflow, sediment storage, and riparian ecosystems in the southern Colorado Front Range. And with the fifth chapter, explore the impacts of mining and population growth on water resources in the upper Arkansas River valley from Pikes Peak to Ca√±on City.&#xD;FLD078, 5 chapters, ISBN 9780813700786 &#xD;list price $45.00, member price $36.00</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:description>
         <xmp:CreateDate>2026-09-24T10:34:46-04:00</xmp:CreateDate>
         <xmp:MetadataDate>2026-09-24T10:34:55-04:00</xmp:MetadataDate>
         <xmp:ModifyDate>2026-09-24T10:34:55-04:00</xmp:ModifyDate>
         <xmp:CreatorTool>Adobe InDesign 20.5 (Macintosh)</xmp:CreatorTool>
